# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
#
# Without this file, `docker build` uploads the ENTIRE directory to the
# builder -- including secrets.env (which holds the real Neo / FileBrowser /
# proxy passwords) and .git. The Dockerfile never COPYs them, but they still
# cross the wire and end up in the builder's cache.
#
# The image is built by GitHub Actions, so the context is uploaded to
# GitHub's builders on every run. This file is the thing that stops your
# passwords from going there.

# secrets and local state
secrets.env
*.rendered.yaml
rendered*.yaml
.sdl.rendered.yaml
.env
*.db

# vcs
.git
.gitignore
.github

# docs / tooling that the image does not need
README.md
*.md
build.sh
verify.sh
deploy-test.sh
watch-gpus.sh

# runtime dirs
work/
logs/

# editor cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
